    val TOFU_BOWLS = "Jump to Recipe   Print Recipe\nCrispy Gochujang Tofu Bowls\nThese sticky, spicy tofu bowls come together in about 40 minutes and reheat beautifully for lunch.\n★★★★★ 4.9 from 212 reviews\nPrep Time: 15 mins   Cook Time: 25 mins\nServings: 3\nAdvertisement\nIngredients\n▢ 1 (14 oz) block extra-firm tofu, pressed\n▢ 2 tbsp cornstarch\n▢ 1/4 tsp salt\nFor the sauce:\n▢ 3 tbsp gochujang\n▢ 2 tbsp honey\n▢ 1½ tbsp soy sauce\n▢ 1 tbsp rice vinegar\n▢ 2 cloves garlic, grated\n▢ 1 tsp toasted sesame oil\nTo serve:\n▢ 2 cups cooked jasmine rice\n▢ 1 small cucumber, thinly sliced\n▢ 2 scallions, sliced\n▢ Sesame seeds, to garnish\nInstructions\nPress the tofu for 15 minutes, then tear it into bite-sized pieces.\nToss the tofu with the cornstarch and salt until every piece is coated.\nPan-fry in 2 tbsp neutral oil over medium-high heat, turning occasionally, for 10 to 12 minutes until crisp on all sides.\nWhisk the gochujang, honey, soy sauce, rice vinegar, garlic and sesame oil in a small bowl.\nLower the heat, pour in the sauce and toss for 2 minutes until the tofu is glossy and sticky.\nDivide the rice between bowls, top with the tofu, cucumber and scallions, and finish with sesame seeds.\nNotes\nLeftovers keep for 3 days in the fridge.\nDid you make this recipe? Tag us!"

    val LEMON_ORZO = "Skip to content\nHome » Recipes » Dinner\nOne-Pot Lemon Orzo with Spinach\nCreamy without any cream, ready in about 25 minutes, and only one pot to wash.\nYield: 4 servings\nTotal Time: 25 minutes\nPin Recipe\nINGREDIENTS\n2 tablespoons butter\n1 shallot, finely chopped\n2 garlic cloves, minced\n1 ½ cups orzo\n3 ½ cups chicken broth\n1 lemon, zested and juiced\n3 handfuls baby spinach\n½ cup grated parmesan\nSalt & black pepper, to taste\nINSTRUCTIONS\n1. Melt the butter in a wide pot over medium heat and cook the shallot for 3 minutes until soft.\n2. Add the garlic and orzo and toast, stirring, for 2 minutes.\n3. Pour in the broth, bring to a boil, then simmer for 10-12 minutes, stirring often, until the orzo is tender and most of the liquid is absorbed.\n4. Stir in the lemon zest, juice and spinach until wilted, about 1 minute.\n5. Take off the heat, stir through the parmesan and season. Rest for 2 minutes to thicken.\nNutrition\nCalories: 412kcal\nShare this: Facebook Pinterest Email"
